[1003]={["atomIDs"]={"1003:description:1-112","1003:description:117-154","1003:description:156-183","1003:description:185-209","1003:description:211-223","1003:description:225-259","1003:description:261-269","1003:description:271-279","1003:description:281-355","1003:description:357-377","1003:description:379-391","1003:description:393-402","1003:description:407-459","1003:description:461-499","1003:objective:1-110"},["opening"]="The final directions came through boiling noises and a wavering voice. Wizbang placed Buzzbox 525 far south beside the road, near a fence and bushes; its materials had to come from grizzled thistle bears.",["pending"]="{actor} would collect four Grizzled Scalps and place them in Buzzbox 525.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Buzzbox 525 with four Grizzled Scalps.",["sourceHash"]="a27a1a9496dc48c522d26a438e631b80413b6d5bc7aaa5e8dbd236a174a4cd65",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1004]={["aftermath"]="Hamuul emphasized the Circle's ties beyond political and racial divisions.",["atomIDs"]={"1004:description:1-18","1004:description:23-135","1004:description:138-303","1004:description:308-380","1004:description:383-483","1004:objective:1-144"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"1004:completion:1-14","1004:completion:19-169","1004:completion:171-284","1004:completion:289-381","1004:completion:383-454"},["opening"]="Balthazad announced the Circle's search for proxies beyond the familiar Kalimdor routes. Hamuul could explain the work in the dangerous wastes west of Tanaris.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to answer the call on Elder Rise.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Hamuul.",["sourceHash"]="5a716d801cfc2a793691ad480c569644f768df53f2255b74757460cc25b69c04",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1007]={["atomIDs"]={"1007:description:1-35","1007:description:40-190","1007:description:193-256","1007:description:261-299","1007:description:301-330","1007:description:335-440","1007:description:443-505","1007:objective:1-72"},["opening"]="Naga drove Talen from his boat above the drowned ruins of Zoram. During his escape he lost the ancient statuette that drew him to the strand, and now asked for it to be recovered along the northern coast.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover the Ancient Statuette for Talen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the Ancient Statuette to Talen.",["sourceHash"]="f1cb0bc84bac5365f39ba5f208fa08385334ac7d3678290b9f4ba4570a8d1806",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1009]={["atomIDs"]={"1009:description:1-110","1009:description:115-152","1009:description:155-238","1009:description:243-307","1009:description:312-381","1009:description:384-420","1009:objective:1-55"},["opening"]="The statuette's lock needed the Ring of Zoram, once held by the drowned city's rulers. Talen said naga had found it, and pointed toward their leader Ruuzel on the island at Zoram's northern edge.",["pending"]="{actor} would retrieve the Ring of Zoram for Talen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Ring of Zoram to Talen.",["sourceHash"]="cd8366c7d02152604873277495f6384041404e74abd18aae2b9f4cac181a4b54",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1011]={["atomIDs"]={"1011:description:1-107","1011:description:110-189","1011:description:192-212","1011:description:217-352","1011:description:355-414","1011:description:417-442","1011:description:445-480","1011:objective:1-62"},["opening"]="Kayneth suspected the Forsaken of bringing disease into Ashenvale. A camp near Dor'Danil produced bottled poisons and illnesses; stealing one bottle might let him test what they intended.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover a Bottle of Disease for Kayneth.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered a Bottle of Disease to Kayneth Stillwind.",["sourceHash"]="f9bfa6651d92897ee71909daa78ebd2c7cdf5bdf0f044834ec5d40ee68263c22",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1012]={["aftermath"]="Kayneth said the barrows' anguish had lessened. He remembered the destroyed spirits as victims and hoped the remaining maddened dead might yet find peace.",["atomIDs"]={"1012:description:1-61","1012:description:64-132","1012:description:134-156","1012:description:159-227","1012:description:232-418","1012:description:423-449","1012:objective:1-119"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"1012:completion:1-89","1012:completion:94-196","1012:completion:198-275"},["opening"]="Kayneth described a vision of Dor'Danil's druids poisoned by the Forsaken and left as maddened spirits. He called for their former leaders to be destroyed in hope that their spirits might one day find peace.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall and Mavoris Cloudsbreak.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against the three named druids and returned to Kayneth.",["sourceHash"]="e14da351eb73371793cb7ce01e49cac2273bf3590cde639fae50ef29da4d07d5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1013]={["aftermath"]="Bel'dugur added the book to his collection and judged Ur's conscience a weakness that had limited his power. That was the keeper's account of the mage's failure against the Scourge.",["atomIDs"]={"1013:description:1-94","1013:description:97-213","1013:description:215-249","1013:description:254-293","1013:description:296-361","1013:objective:1-78"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"1013:completion:1-10","1013:completion:12-77","1013:completion:79-147","1013:completion:149-216","1013:completion:221-291"},["opening"]="Bel'dugur prized the studies of Ur, a Dalaran mage from before the Scourge's coming. The book in Shadowfang would interest unnamed Forsaken parties as well as enrich his collection.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to retrieve the Book of Ur for Bel'dugur.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Book of Ur to Keeper Bel'dugur.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3440969046934676bd4408086ad7c64be524abe62c6520b8c6a0e200d6724548",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1014]={["aftermath"]="Dawnweaver credited Arugal's defeat with ending the wizard's grip on Silverpine and called it service to the Dark Lady.",["atomIDs"]={"1014:description:1-40","1014:description:42-134","1014:description:139-189","1014:description:191-269","1014:description:274-355","1014:description:357-391","1014:objective:1-68"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"1014:completion:1-70","1014:completion:72-119","1014:completion:121-152"},["opening"]="Dawnweaver considered Arugal the barrier to securing Silverpine for the Dark Lady. The wizard still occupied Shadowfang, and a head returned to the Sepulcher was the demanded proof of his end.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Arugal and return his head to Dawnweaver.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Arugal assignment and delivered his head to Dalar Dawnweaver.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="7b06a47a989b387aebe11f4b16049df4fb753f4a48bc87d0c316d3a21a23cbb1",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1015]={["atomIDs"]={"1015:description:1-18","1015:description:23-135","1015:description:138-303","1015:description:308-380","1015:description:383-461","1015:objective:1-146"},["opening"]="A city announcement called for proxies to explore Kalimdor's dangerous western reaches. Fandral in Darnassus could explain the Cenarion Circle's request beyond the public appeal.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to consult Fandral about the Circle's call.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm about the frontier appeal.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="d9ff52c7c0abfd667ea210dde21906e5175b50de408b1cd526ffbc6d6aa7bf43",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1016]={["atomIDs"]={"1016:description:1-76","1016:description:78-191","1016:description:196-252","1016:description:254-376","1016:description:378-436","1016:description:438-499","1016:objective:1-71","1016:objective:73-164"},["opening"]="Velene provided a divining scroll to identify the water elementals' creator. Five intact bracers could focus its magic, after which the resulting scroll had to return to Silverwind Refuge.",["pending"]="{actor} would use the Divining Scroll with five Intact Elemental Bracers and bring Velene the result.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the bracer divination and delivered the Divined Scroll to Velene Starstrike.",["sourceHash"]="a65a8fdb31b05c2e1f2b0a4c8395781032aae4eecb982eabfa84901333fdce80",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1017]={["atomIDs"]={"1017:description:1-91","1017:description:93-137","1017:description:139-221","1017:description:226-289","1017:description:291-389","1017:description:394-427","1017:description:429-478","1017:objective:1-93"},["opening"]="Velene named Sarilus Foulborne as the undead mage capable of defiling so many elementals. She believed he waited on Dreadmist Peak in the Barrens and warned that pursuing him meant entering Horde territory.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Sarilus Foulborne and bring his head to Velene.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against Sarilus Foulborne and delivered his head to Velene.",["sourceHash"]="a3b66ebe9d2772b351cac6a9363b994027504ceb107a35b24adb3d1063e7757f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1018]={["aftermath"]="Hamuul emphasized the Circle's connection across political divisions.",["atomIDs"]={"1018:description:1-18","1018:description:23-135","1018:description:138-303","1018:description:308-380","1018:description:383-483","1018:objective:1-144"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"1018:completion:1-14","1018:completion:19-169","1018:completion:171-284","1018:completion:289-381","1018:completion:383-454"},["opening"]="The call in Orgrimmar sought honorable proxies for a forbidden western wasteland. Gorlach directed interested fighters to the Circle's senior representative in Thunder Bluff.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to answer Gorlach's frontier call.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Hamuul.",["sourceHash"]="56c44fad9e2fdeeb584fff0065dbf0e03f9dcf89f80c4e019a1af04486c7cb10",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1019]={["atomIDs"]={"1019:description:1-18","1019:description:23-135","1019:description:138-303","1019:description:308-380","1019:description:383-461","1019:objective:1-146"},["opening"]="Hammerfall carried the Circle's appeal for willing explorers. Beyond Tanaris lay a forbidden wasteland, and those considering the work were directed to Fandral for its terms.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Fandral about the Kalimdor expedition.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm about the Circle's frontier work.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="188ce65fe4625539f91f1b5e780f62e7e5323fa9315508bf09a5fc4c25e735c1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1021]={["atomIDs"]={"1021:description:1-55","1021:description:57-123","1021:description:125-184","1021:description:189-214","1021:description:216-296","1021:description:298-324","1021:description:326-377","1021:objective:1-22"},["opening"]="Illiyana's sisters left to reclaim the Branch of Cenarius from satyrs and had been gone two days. Anilia led them toward a ruined temple in Xavian, where the search for the missing dryads had to begin.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find Anilia in Xavian.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Anilia in Xavian.",["sourceHash"]="60d315288b851af1178c735d05cc2f75583a5e25c57c390fffe4d23d5fc872c1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1022]={["atomIDs"]={"1022:description:1-143","1022:description:145-214","1022:description:219-333","1022:description:335-405","1022:description:407-502","1022:objective:1-118"},["opening"]="Wolf-men occupied the ruined shrine of Mel'Thandris near Felwood, their calls giving the Howling Vale its name. Melyria hoped the shrine's tome could explain their arrival while demonic threats still pressed the border.",["pending"]="{actor} would study the Tome of Mel'Thandris and report to Melyria.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the tome study and returned to Melyria Frostshadow.",["sourceHash"]="4fe69627c8f14167520b33490bfb87409d6131fc422eb44d1b15ac13bf105937",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1023]={["atomIDs"]={"1023:description:1-95","1023:description:100-152","1023:description:157-218","1023:description:220-256","1023:description:258-287","1023:objective:1-87"},["opening"]="Teronis's journal survived beside his body, but the gem remained missing. His search had to be completed near the lake before the journal and Glowing Gem could return to Raene; murlocs might hold the stone.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find the Glowing Gem and take it with Teronis' Journal to Raene.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Glowing Gem and Teronis' Journal to Raene.",["sourceHash"]="7f27fbb3b1d32b0ec56775fc8c2849f7a85b0d6bcdfe2cc1bcba82bf1f72fd4a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1024]={["atomIDs"]={"1024:description:1-175","1024:description:177-235","1024:description:237-335","1024:description:340-400","1024:description:402-414","1024:description:419-503","1024:objective:1-49"},["opening"]="Teronis's notes pointed toward the other pieces of Dartol's rod. Raene directed the work to Shael'dryn at the moonwell east of Iris Lake, with the recovered gem kept close for reconstruction.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to seek Shael'dryn at the moonwell with the gem.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} found Shael'dryn at the moonwell.",["sourceHash"]="2cdad968d3e45338e041f51946bd2239dfc03596bc784090f7e912e1d29811cc",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1025]={["atomIDs"]={"1025:description:1-130","1025:description:135-229","1025:description:231-325","1025:description:330-437","1025:description:442-487","1025:description:489-499","1025:objective:1-131"},["opening"]="Raene offered a separate defense of the eastern road before the moonwell journey. Foulweald furbolgs south of the road had attacked travelers, and she called for action against their fighters, totemics, ursas and den watcher.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Raene's specified Foulweald assignment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against one Den Watcher, two Ursas, ten Totemics and twelve Warriors and returned to Raene.",["sourceHash"]="9c4766da2a7a3cd18be1ef310fc1e50287c0ee5d28d711d188fb17b2daa39370",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1026]={["atomIDs"]={"1026:description:1-32","1026:description:37-134","1026:description:136-186","1026:description:191-300","1026:description:305-376","1026:description:378-461","1026:description:463-502","1026:objective:1-95"},["opening"]="Shael'dryn knew another rod piece lay locked in a chest near the Felwood border. A corrupted treant carried its wooden key, leaving both key and hidden glade to be found before the piece could be returned.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find the Wooden Key and recover Dartol's rod piece for Shael'dryn.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the key-and-rod-piece assignment and returned to Shael'dryn.",["sourceHash"]="8e0391d25a66747e7d6635f53b7e2581cfc1a792d50753f3ddbd66c7a7ab0fd2",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1027]={["aftermath"]="Shael'dryn acknowledged the final piece and turned her attention to repairing the rod. Recovering its fragments had opened the next task rather than finished its restoration.",["atomIDs"]={"1027:description:1-80","1027:description:82-114","1027:description:116-157","1027:description:162-233","1027:description:235-351","1027:description:353-400","1027:description:405-490","1027:objective:1-78"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"1027:completion:1-26","1027:completion:28-47","1027:completion:49-62","1027:completion:67-121"},["opening"]="The final rod piece was entrusted to Dor'Danil's druids, now dead. Shael'dryn knew where they sheltered east of the Barrens road but not where they hid it; recovering that last piece would allow reconstruction.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find the final piece of Dartol's Rod and bring it to Shael'dryn.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the final piece of Dartol's Rod to Shael'dryn.",["sourceHash"]="c34086167f80acad7451349ecbf43d2970ce09d030f0851c8e98711ed8f88abf",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1028]={["aftermath"]="When the shrine's glow faded, the re-enchanted rod remained in its basin. The artifact's restoration had reached the point Shael'dryn had sought.",["atomIDs"]={"1028:description:1-30","1028:description:32-62","1028:description:64-148","1028:description:153-261","1028:description:266-362","1028:description:364-430","1028:description:435-480","1028:description:482-499","1028:description:501-505","1028:objective:1-51"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"1028:completion:1-80"},["opening"]="Reconstruction was easier than restoring the rod's power. Shael'dryn sent the completed artifact to a shrine hidden in the mountains southeast of the moonwell, where it could be re-enchanted.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find the hidden shrine and re-enchant Dartol's Rod.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the re-enchantment assignment at the hidden shrine.",["sourceHash"]="c6ae2b49a0403f3038e086bad0e889dc881e7edf4820992f28f5016b97151a09",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1029]={["atomIDs"]={"1029:description:1-62","1029:description:64-116","1029:description:121-134","1029:objective:1-40"},["opening"]="Shael'dryn sent the inquiry back to Astranaar. With the rod finished, Raene had to decide how its recovered power could serve the forest.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return to Raene with news of the completed rod.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.",["sourceHash"]="39efbfe676997804c8eba28605b30c838829337785adfb1257d64c1f1ddd1c6d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1030]={["atomIDs"]={"1030:description:1-58","1030:description:63-168","1030:description:170-195","1030:description:200-348","1030:description:350-455","1030:description:460-511","1030:objective:1-97"},["opening"]="Raene was unsure of Dartol's intended plan or even the form his rod granted. She thought its transformation might allow contact with an uncorrupted furbolg and suggested searching southeast of Mystral Lake.",["pending"]="{actor} would use Dartol's Rod of Transformation to speak with an uncorrupted furbolg.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the transformed meeting with the uncorrupted furbolg Krolg.",["sourceHash"]="9bc44ba7d94e6f385f8cf57b3bda881d801cc2bd35003245098b82d790b6aa3c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[1031]={["atomIDs"]={"1031:description:1-60","1031:description:62-179","1031:description:181-199","1031:description:201-315","1031:objective:1-76"},["opening"]="Anilia's final indication pointed north toward Geltharis, who had taken the Branch of Cenarius. Recovering the branch for Illiyana was the unfinished purpose left by the dying dryad.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Geltharis and return the Branch of Cenarius to Illiyana.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against Geltharis and delivered the Branch of Cenarius to Illiyana.",["sourceHash"]="bd776a9bb44d01b7c7ddae4cc22ac3f741e37def10742f08e3f0b433266cce1a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
